# what: The square of an int16_t sample is formed in int, which on a part with a 16 bit int overflows for any sample past 181.
#
# Every host here has a 32 bit int, so Rms_Test passes with this in place and
# always will; only a build for a 16 bit int can see it, and the run time
# overflow is not a warning even there. scripts/int16.sh pins it by the helper
# the multiply calls.
#
# Applied by scripts/mutate.sh, which requires the FIND block to match
# exactly once and the named test to fail because of it.
FILE src/filter/rms.c
TEST scripts/int16.sh
--- FIND
    square = ( ( int32_t ) sample ) * ( ( int32_t ) sample );
--- REPLACE
    square = sample * sample;
--- END
